@startuml
title Media Lab Manager - Database Workflow

actor Backend
participant "Database facade" as DB
database SQLite
participant "Audit log" as Audit
participant "Outbox" as Outbox

== Database initialization ==

Backend -> DB: Database(path)
DB -> SQLite: Open database
DB -> SQLite: Create missing tables
DB -> SQLite: Migrate listings.images
DB -> SQLite: Migrate equipment.listing_id
DB --> Backend: Ready

== Example data ==

Backend -> DB: Run seed_test_equipment.py
DB -> SQLite: Insert example users/settings
DB -> SQLite: Insert listings with images JSON
DB -> SQLite: Insert individual equipment units
DB -> SQLite: Insert sample requests and lifecycle records
DB --> Backend: Seed summary

== Catalog display ==

Backend -> DB: get_listings(filters)
DB -> SQLite: Read listings and linked equipment
SQLite --> DB: Quantity, status, unit IDs, images
DB --> Backend: Catalog dictionaries
note right
  images is returned as a list of objects:
  url, alt, attribution
end note

== Create request ==

Backend -> DB: create_request(request data)
DB -> SQLite: Check requester
DB -> SQLite: Check equipment exists and is available
DB -> SQLite: Check overlapping time windows
alt Invalid or unavailable
  DB --> Backend: Error
else Available
  DB -> SQLite: Insert request and request_items
  DB -> SQLite: Mark equipment requested
  DB -> SQLite: Insert pickup/return windows
  DB -> Audit: Record request.created
  DB -> Outbox: Emit request.created
  DB --> Backend: Request with items and windows
end

== Approval or cancellation ==

Backend -> DB: approve_request / reject_request / cancel_request
DB -> SQLite: Update request and item statuses
DB -> SQLite: Update equipment status
DB -> Audit: Record status change
DB -> Outbox: Emit request event
DB --> Backend: Updated request

== Pickup ==

Backend -> DB: record_pickup(requestId)
DB -> SQLite: Create/update return records
DB -> SQLite: Mark request items and equipment picked_up
DB -> Audit: Record pickup.confirmed
DB -> Outbox: Emit pickup.confirmed
DB --> Backend: Updated request

== Return and damage ==

Backend -> DB: record_return(requestId, condition, damageFlag)
DB -> SQLite: Record return condition
DB -> SQLite: Mark item returned or damaged
DB -> SQLite: Mark equipment available or damaged
DB -> Audit: Record return.recorded
DB -> Outbox: Emit return.recorded
DB --> Backend: Updated request

Backend -> DB: record_damage(requestItemId, description)
DB -> SQLite: Insert damage report
DB -> SQLite: Mark request item and equipment damaged
DB -> Audit: Record damage.reported
DB -> Outbox: Emit damage.reported
DB --> Backend: Damage report

== Integration events ==

Backend -> DB: get_outbox(limit)
DB -> SQLite: Read unpublished events
SQLite --> DB: Event rows with JSON payloads
DB --> Backend: Event list
Backend -> DB: mark_events_published(ids)
DB -> SQLite: Set published_at timestamps

== Shutdown ==

Backend -> DB: close()
DB -> SQLite: Close connection

@enduml
